    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "heading": "What the numbers mean",
      "items": [
        "CLI comparison is process wall time plus peak RSS for freshly built gowkhtmltopdf versus the installed wkhtmltopdf binary.",
        "WeasyPrint and Puppeteer use the same generated report fixture; Puppeteer RSS includes the Node driver and headless Chrome process tree.",
        "In-process go test -bench rows measure conversion inside the test process. B/op is cumulative allocation traffic.",
        "The public Go library rows call Document.WritePDF and ImageDocument.WriteImage directly. The approximately 70x landing claim is 259 ms divided by 3.77 ms at 2 pages, using the wkhtmltopdf CLI as the baseline.",
        "The report fixture is testdata/golden/benchmarks/templates/report.html.tmpl with 20 invoice rows per requested page.",
        "Page islands (convert.NewBenchmarkPDFRequest) are a benchmark-only opt-in. Ordinary CLI and library requests stay on the generic path.",
        "Full matrices, historical snapshots, and raw go test rows live in testdata/golden/benchmarks/ and documentation/performance.md."
